# scripts/check-docs-populated.ts judges whether a harness's declared docs directories hold authored documentation:
# enough prose on one non-generated page, and that same page naming a declared process, role and task.
# Each Scenario names the test that executes it.
Feature: A harness's documentation is populated, not a title and a list of links

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::proseWords::a_line_that_is_only_a_link_contributes_nothing
  Scenario: A page of link-only lines measures almost no prose
    Given a markdown page of a heading and three bullet links
    When its prose words are counted
    Then the count is under 5

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::proseWords::front_matter,_comments_and_code_fences_are_not_prose
  Scenario: Front matter, comments and code fences are not counted as prose
    Given a markdown page with front matter, an HTML comment, a code fence and the line "Real words here."
    When its prose words are counted
    Then the count is 3

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::proseWords::markup_is_stripped_from_html,_and_script_and_style_with_it
  Scenario: HTML markup, script and style are stripped before counting
    Given an HTML page with a style block, a script block and "<p>Three real words</p>"
    When its prose words are counted as HTML
    Then the count is 3

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::looksGenerated_—_anchored,_because_both_loose_forms_measured_wrong::prose_ABOUT_a_generator_is_not_a_generated_page
  Scenario: Prose that mentions a generator is not a generated page
    Given the text "the SVG is generated by `bun run cat render:bpmn`."
    When it is tested for looking generated
    Then it does not look generated

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::looksGenerated_—_anchored,_because_both_loose_forms_measured_wrong::the_viewers'_own_marker_is_recognised,_on_its_own_line
  Scenario: The viewers' SCOPE marker marks a page generated only on its own line
    Given the line 'var SCOPE = "beans";'
    Then it looks generated
    And a sentence quoting 'var SCOPE = "x";' in the middle of prose does not look generated

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::looksGenerated_—_anchored,_because_both_loose_forms_measured_wrong::the_two_whole_phrases_are_recognised
  Scenario: The "Generated by" and "Generated from … do not edit" phrases are recognised
    Given a line starting "Generated by scripts/state-visualizer.ts. Do not hand-edit"
    And a line starting "Generated from" and ending "do not edit here."
    Then each looks generated

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::a_harness_whose_only_page_is_a_link_list_is_THIN
  Scenario: A harness whose only page is a link list is thin
    Given a harness whose declared "h/pages" directory holds one index.md of a heading and two links
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "thin"
    And the detail mentions "words of prose"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::a_page_that_says_something_is_POPULATED,_and_it_is_named_as_the_evidence
  Scenario: A page with enough prose makes the harness populated and is named as the evidence
    Given a harness whose "h/pages/index.md" holds a long run of prose
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "populated"
    And the best page is "h/pages/index.md"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::a_GENERATED_page_never_carries_a_harness,_however_long_it_is
  Scenario: A generated page never makes a harness populated, however long
    Given a harness whose only page is an index.html of long prose carrying the viewers' SCOPE marker
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "thin"
    And one page is counted as generated
    And the detail says "an index is not the documentation"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::a_declared_directory_that_is_not_there_is_UNKNOWN,_never_thin
  Scenario: A declared docs directory that is absent is unknown, never thin
    Given a harness that declares "h/pages" but has no such directory
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "unknown"
    And the detail cites "dh4f"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::an_unreadable_page_is_UNKNOWN,_not_a_thin_verdict
  Scenario: An unreadable page makes the verdict unknown
    # Gap: when the permission plant does not take (e.g. running as root) the test only logs and asserts nothing
    Given a harness with a long index.md and a locked.md made unreadable
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "unknown"
    And at least one page is counted as ambiguous

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::assess::dot-prefixed_directories_are_not_searched
  Scenario: Dot-prefixed directories are not searched
    Given a harness whose only long page sits under "h/pages/.cache"
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the verdict is "thin"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_page_naming_a_declared_process,_role_and_task_is_populated
  Scenario: A page naming a declared process, role and task passes the subject half
    Given declared processes, roles and tasks including "Adjudication", "Author" and "L1 completeness gate"
    And a page naming all three
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "populated"
    And the found process, role and task are "Adjudication", "Author" and "L1 completeness gate"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::one_string_that_is_both_a_process_and_a_task_scores_ONE,_not_two
  Scenario: A name that is both a process and a task counts once
    Given "Adjudication" is declared as both a process and a task
    And a page saying only "Adjudication is how we decide."
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "thin"
    And both the found process and the found task are "Adjudication"
    And the detail says the page names 1 of the three as distinct names

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_process_and_a_role_but_no_distinct_task_is_thin,_and_the_detail_says_how_close
  Scenario: A process and a role with no distinct task is thin, and the detail counts two
    Given a page saying "Adjudication, run by an Author."
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "thin"
    And the detail says the page names 2 of the three as distinct names
    And the detail does not mention "a task"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::declaring_none_of_the_three_is_UNKNOWN,_never_a_pass
  Scenario: A harness declaring no processes, roles or tasks is unknown
    Given no declared processes, roles or tasks and a page of 400 words
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "unknown"
    And the declared counts are all 0

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::declaring_processes_and_tasks_but_no_roles_is_still_UNKNOWN,_and_names_which_half_is_missing
  Scenario: Declaring processes and tasks but no roles is unknown and says roles are missing
    Given one declared process and one declared task but no roles, and no pages
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "unknown"
    And the detail mentions "no roles"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_name_under_four_characters_is_dropped_rather_than_matched
  Scenario: Names shorter than four characters are dropped
    Given declared names "BA", "QA" and "Do" only
    And a page about baking and quality where "we do things"
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "unknown"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::subjects_are_resolved_from_the_DECLARATION_—_processes,_roles_and_tasks,_each_from_its_own_graph_typology
  Scenario: Subjects are resolved from the instance declaration's graph typologies
    Given an instance declaring a "pages" docs directory, a "flows" processes directory with a BPMN and a "lanes" scenarios directory with a role graph
    When its subjects are read
    Then the processes include "Adjudication"
    And the tasks include "L1 completeness gate"
    And the roles include both the title "Author" and the id "author"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_LONG_page_about_nothing_plus_a_SHORT_page_naming_all_three_is_NOT_a_subject_pass
  Scenario: A long page about nothing plus a short page naming all three does not pass the subject half
    Given the planted instance with a long filler page and a short page naming all three
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the prose verdict is "populated"
    And the subject verdict is "thin"
    And the declared counts are 1 process, 2 roles and 1 task
    When the short page is made long enough while still naming all three
    Then the subject verdict is "populated" with page "pages/short.md"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_role_graph_that_does_not_parse_is_UNREADABLE,_not_absent,_and_the_detail_says_so
  Scenario: A role graph that fails to parse is reported unreadable, not absent
    Given the planted instance whose roles.json lacks the required actorKinds
    When its subjects are read
    Then there are no roles and one unreadable entry naming roles.json
    When the harness is assessed with a long page
    Then the subject verdict is "unknown"
    And the detail says "could not read" and not "declares no"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::a_short_page_naming_all_three_is_not_eligible_—_one_page_must_satisfy_both_halves
  Scenario: A short page naming all three is not eligible for the subject half
    Given a pages directory with a long filler page and a short page naming all three, and no declaration
    When the harness is assessed
    Then the prose verdict is "populated"
    And the subject verdict is "unknown"
    And assessing the subject over the long page alone gives "thin"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::subject_—_the_processes/roles/tasks_half::among_pages_that_qualify,_the_one_with_the_most_prose_is_named
  Scenario: Among qualifying pages, the one with the most prose is named
    Given "docs/ar/short.md" and "docs/real.md" both naming all three, the second with 300 more words
    When the subject half is assessed
    Then the verdict is "populated"
    And the named page is "docs/real.md"

  @test:scripts/tests/check-docs-populated.test.ts::harnessesWithDocs_—_a_docs_directory_built_at_publish_is_not_authored_documentation::an_instance_whose_only_docs_directory_is_built_at_publish_drops_out;_one_with_an_authored_docs_directory_stays
  Scenario: An instance whose only docs directory is built at publish is not checked
    Given an instance "built" whose docs directory is declared built at publish
    And an instance "authored" with an ordinary docs directory
    When the harnesses with docs are listed
    Then "authored" is listed
    And "built" is not
